@@ -0,0 +1,2462 @@
+From: Abdalla Ashry <abdallah.ashry@hotmail.com>
+Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:32:46 +0200
+Subject: rockchip: add support for FriendlyARM NanoPi R28S
+
+Hardware specification:
+- SoC: Rockchip RK3528A (4x Cortex-A53)
+- RAM: 1GB LPDDR4X
+- Storage: optional eMMC, microSD slot
+- Ethernet: 1x 1GbE RTL8211F (WAN), 1x 1GbE RTL8111H via PCIe (LAN)
+- WiFi/BT: AIC8800D80 SDIO module (no driver yet)
+- USB: 1x USB-C (power input, USB 2.0 OTG / maskrom)
+- RTC: HYM8563
+- LEDs: 1x SYS (red), 1x WAN (green), 1x LAN (green)
+- Buttons: 1x user (K2_USR, used as reset), 1x MASK
+- UART: USB-C debug port (CH340E), 1500000 8N1
+- Power: 5V via USB-C
+
+Devicetree:
+Backport the upstream FriendlyElec NanoPi R28S devicetree from v7.4
+together with the patch that moves the parts shared with the NanoPi
+Zero2 into rk3528-nanopi.dtsi. The last hunk of the split patch is
+adapted, as v6.18 lacks the USB nodes upstream has at the end of the
+NanoPi Zero2 devicetree.
+
+On top of the upstream devicetree, the user button is set as reset
+button. The SYS LED is used as OpenWrt status LED and its heartbeat
+trigger and default-on state are dropped. This is done in the shared
+RK3528 NanoPi dtsi, so the NanoPi Zero2 gets the same status LED
+handling.
+
+U-Boot:
+Add a U-Boot target for the NanoPi R28S. U-Boot 2026.10 lacks the
+board, so backport the RK3528 watchdog/USB devicetree nodes and the
+NanoPi Zero2 USB ports from U-Boot next, add the Linux v7.4 NanoPi
+RK3528 split and R28S devicetrees to dts/upstream, and apply the
+pending U-Boot patches adding the R28S defconfig.
+
+MAC addresses:
+- WAN (eth0): provided by U-Boot (generated from the SoC OTP cpuid)
+- LAN (eth1): WAN MAC + 1, as the RTL8111H has no programmed MAC
+
+Installation (microSD):
+1. Write the image to a microSD card:
+   gunzip -c openwrt-*-nanopi-r28s-squashfs-sysupgrade.img.gz | \
+     dd of=/dev/sdX bs=1M conv=fsync
+2. Insert the card and power on the board.
+3. Later upgrades can use sysupgrade.
+
+Tested: Ethernet (WAN/LAN), LEDs, reset button, microSD boot,
+sysupgrade.
+
+Signed-off-by: Abdalla Ashry <abdallah.ashry@hotmail.com>
+
