+diff --git a/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/109-1-arm64-dts-rockchip-Split-out-the-common-NanoPi-RK3528-parts.patch b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/109-1-arm64-dts-rockchip-Split-out-the-common-NanoPi-RK3528-parts.patch
+new file mode 100644
+index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1cab5b96ce5d30b227017553b2dae787808ada0c
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/109-1-arm64-dts-rockchip-Split-out-the-common-NanoPi-RK3528-parts.patch
+@@ -0,0 +1,661 @@
++From fdb087806e808ccc4963e2e5225fe16581ecb421 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: 安容 <HystericalDragons@proton.me>
++Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:28:18 +0800
++Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: Split out the common NanoPi RK3528
++ parts
++MIME-Version: 1.0
++Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
++Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
++
++The FriendlyElec NanoPi Zero2 and the NanoPi R28S share their power
++tree, storage, RGMII Ethernet, RTC, LEDs and debug console. Move those
++parts into rk3528-nanopi.dtsi so the NanoPi R28S can reuse them, and
++leave only the board specific nodes in the NanoPi Zero2 devicetree.
++
++Both boards drive a green LED from GPIO4_PB1, but give it a different
++purpose, so the common file describes the LED itself and each board
++adds the function, trigger and default state. While moving the LED pins
++give them the usual _pin suffix, which frees the led1 label for the LED
++node.
++
++Suggested-by: Chukun Pan <amadeus@jmu.edu.cn>
++Signed-off-by: 安容 <HystericalDragons@proton.me>
++Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260919-r28s-upstream-v7-2-e80a6f8ef521@proton.me
++Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner <heiko@sntech.de>
++---
++ .../arm64/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-zero2.dts    | 290 +----------------
++ .../src/arm64/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi.dtsi     | 291 ++++++++++++++++++
